    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and rewired everything that keys off the household. All changes are in the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**Core derivation**\n- `HouseholdId.of(lastName, postcode)` \u2014 now hashes `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (normalized last name = trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase) and returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256. Previously it hashed `lastName + '\\n' + normalizedAddress`.\n- `IdentityKey.of(...)` \u2014 its household component now uses postcode instead of address (last param renamed accordingly).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the `householdId` and `identityKey` derived mappings now pass `owner.getPostcode()` instead of `owner.getAddress()`, so the value returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` is the postcode-based id.\n\n**Duplicate block (`RejectDuplicateOwner`)** \u2014 replaced the telephone-collision check with a household check: rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409) when an existing owner shares the same computed `householdId`. A request with `sharesHousehold=true` returns early, bypassing the block (it no longer \"creates a link\" \u2014 the id is derived automatically).\n\n**Soft-match (`DetectPossibleDuplicate`)** \u2014 now keys off `householdId`, and a declared member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is explicitly never flagged (`possibleDuplicate=false`), reading `sharesHousehold` via the published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto request`.\n\n**Household size (`CountHousehold`)** \u2014 counts members by matching computed `householdId` instead of `(lastName, normalizedAddress)`.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` descriptions (`sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) and the stale `AddressNormalizer`/javadoc references.\n\n**Result:** owners with the same last name + postcode share a `householdId`; a second such owner is a 409 household duplicate unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member and not flagged. `AcceptanceTest.coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
